# Copy to .env for local dev: cp .env.example .env
# Vite loads .env / .env.local / .env.[mode] automatically — see
# https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode. Only VITE_-prefixed vars reach the
# browser bundle; this one also doubles as the dev-server proxy target
# (vite.config.ts).

# Where the Leash gateway lives.
#
# Dev (default if unset): the Vite dev server proxies same-origin /api/*
# requests to this URL, sidestepping the gateway's lack of CORS headers.
#   VITE_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:4021
#
# Production: leave this UNSET and have whatever serves the built dist/
# (Vercel/Netlify rewrite, Nginx, Caddy, ...) proxy /api/* to the gateway
# the same way — the app keeps calling same-origin /api and never needs to
# know the gateway's real address. See README.md "Deploying".
#
# Only set this to an absolute URL (https://gateway.example.com) if the
# gateway already sends CORS headers for this frontend's origin — it
# doesn't by default. Doing so bakes the URL into the built JS at build
# time and calls the gateway directly, no proxy needed.
VITE_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:4021
